From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Mark the assertion-only locals of partial_aggregate_pushdown.cpp as used

partial_aggregate_pushdown.cpp declares locals that only D_ASSERT() reads (has_side),
so in a release build, where D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, they are unused
and -Wunused-variable or -Wunused-but-set-variable says so. Each is cast
to void after its declaration, which changes no behavior.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/partial_aggregate_pushdown.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/partial_aggregate_pushdown.cpp
--- a/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/partial_aggregate_pushdown.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/partial_aggregate_pushdown.cpp
@@ -805,6 +805,7 @@ static unique_ptr<LogicalAggregate> DECreateUpperAggregate(Optimizer &optimizer,
 		auto &ref = group->Cast<BoundColumnRefExpression>();
 		idx_t gs;
 		auto has_side = GetExpressionSide(*group, side_bindings, gs);
+		(void)has_side;
 		D_ASSERT(has_side);
 		auto binding = sides[gs].group_map.at(ref.Binding());
 		upper_aggr->groups.push_back(make_uniq<BoundColumnRefExpression>(ref.GetReturnType(), binding));
